---
// ── Build on trust ────────────────────────────────────
---

<section class="section">
  <h2 class="h">Build on trust, extend it forward</h2>
  <p class="section-desc" style="text-align:center;margin-bottom:1.75rem">
    Images are built as layers, and each layer cryptographically binds to the one below it — so one
    trust anchor validates the whole stack.
  </p>
  <div class="steps">
    <div class="step">
      <div class="n">START</div>
      <h3>From a trusted base</h3>
      <p>
        Begin with a base image whose integrity you already vouch for — a shared root others build
        from.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="step">
      <div class="n">EXTEND</div>
      <h3>Add your own layers</h3>
      <p>
        Stack your changes on top. Each layer is a read-only, integrity-protected image bound into
        the chain below it.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="step">
      <div class="n">VERIFY</div>
      <h3>One anchor checks it all</h3>
      <p>
        A single trusted root validates the entire stack. Tamper with any layer and the check fails
        — no trust is lost as you extend.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <p class="illus">
    Shared bases mean common layers are fetched, signed, and scanned once — then reused across every
    image that builds on them.
  </p>
</section>
